nt to quality have consistently enabled me to deliver impactful, enterprise-ready WordPress VIP and PHP solutions.\n\nTOOLS\nVS Code, PhpMyAdmin, JIRA, Github, Postman, Chrome Dev Tool, cPanel, FTP, AWS-S3\n\nDOMAIN\nE-commerce, Health Care, Content Management, Education\nSKILLS\n\nWordPress / WP VIP \n(4/5)\n\nPHP\n(4/5)\n\nGit\n(3.5/5)\n\nSQL / MySQL \n(3.5/5)\n\nHTML, CSS, jQuery\n(3/5)\n\nReact Js\n(3/5)\n\nREST APIs, XML/JSON Parsing\n(3/5)\n\nClient Interaction \n(3/5)\n\n\n\nPROJECTS\nProject 1 - Oct 2021 - Jun 2025\nMedia and Publishing \n\nTools & Technologies\nWordPress VIP, PHP, MySQL, ReactJS, HTML5, CSS, JQuery\n\nTeam Size\n40\n\nRole\nSenior Software Engineer\n\nProject Link\nNDA\n\nAs a Senior Software Engineer on the project, I was responsible for managing all the frontend functionality of the WordPress site. The project was architected around two centralized content HUBs – B2B and B2C – each aligned to different business units and editorial workflows. These HUBs served as the primary interface for content creation and management by editorial teams, and were integrated with multiple delivery sites that surfaced the content to end users.\n\nProject 2 - Dec 2020 - Sept 2021\nData Migration \n\nTools & Technologies\nWordPress VIP, PHP, MySQL\n\nTeam Size\n40\n\nRole\nSoftware Engineer\n\nProject Link\nNDA\n\nAs a Software Engineer/Senior Software Engineer, I developed migration scripts to transfer content from multiple legacy CMS platforms into the WPVIP ecosystem. I ensured data accuracy and consistency during large-scale migrations, optimized performance, and resolved issues. Additionally, I collaborated with cross-functional teams to validate results and deliver a seamless transition.\n\nProject 3 - Jan 2020 - Apr 2020\nTable booking site\n\nTools & Technologies\nWordPress, HTML, MySQL, CSS, React, JQuery\n\nTeam Size\n3\n\nRole\nSenior Software Engineer\n\nProject Link\nNDA\nDeveloped a table booking website for a 5-location hotel chain, enabling u