umentation\n\n\nPROJECTS\nProject 1 - Jan 2025 - Nov 2025\nEngage & GFMS\n\nTools & Technologies:\nSalesforce, JIRA, CSM, Confluence, Sharepoint, TestRail, MS Office\n\nTeam Size: 2-5\n\nRole: QA Lead\n\nProject Description:\nSuite of technology and services for optimizing interactions with Healthcare Professionals (HCPs) and patients, featuring an integrated platform for compliant event management, digital engagement, data analytics, and workflow automation to connect life sciences companies with key stakeholders from molecule to market.\n\nResponsibilities & Achievements:\nLed a QA team of 2-5 testers in an Agile environment, collaborating with development teams to implement a new bug tracking process that reduced resolution time by 20%.\nStreamlined test documentation by creating a centralized repository of 200+ reusable test cases in sharepoint, reducing test preparation time by 30-40% and enabling faster onboarding of new team members.\nDefined test strategy, scope, effort estimation, and resource planning for releases. Reduced production defects by 35–45% through optimized test planning and RCA practices.\nReviewed test cases, test scenarios, and test execution reports prepared by team members. Introduced reusable test suite structure that improved test execution efficiency by 30%.\nPerformed functional, regression, integration, accessibility, and UAT testing.\nIdentified process gaps, implemented QA best practices, and improved test coverage. Earned multiple “PAT ON THE BACK” Awards from clients for successful releases.\nSet up and monitored QA metrics: defect leakage, requirement coverage, execution progress, and release readiness.\nConducted defect triage meetings with product owners, architects, and cross-functional teams (BA, Dev) to clarify requirements and resolve issues.\nSpearheaded the creation of a standardized QA training curriculum and mentorship framework, successfully cross-training all junior analysts on complex proprietary systems and improving team versatility.\n\n\nProject 2 - Feb 2020 - Dec 2024\nHealthcare Interaction Portal\n\nTools & Technologies:\nJIRA, CSM, Confluence, TestRail, MS Office, SSMS\n\nTeam Size: 3\n\nRole: QA Lead\n\nProject Description:\nHIP is Healthcare Provider Interaction Portal which provides functionality to manage the entire HCP Contracting life cycle.It includes Event, Contracting, Details of Expenses, Spend on HCP and Activity, Maintaining FMV.\n\nResponsibilities & Achievements:\nLead a QA team (2 members) ensuring high-quality delivery.\nDefined test strategy, scope, effort estimation, and resource planning for releases. Reduced production defects by 35–45% through optimized test planning and RCA practices.\nSet up and monitored QA metrics: defect leakage, requirement coverage, execution progress, and release readiness.\nConducted defect triage meetings with product owners, architects, and development leads.\nCollaborated with cross-functional teams (BA, Dev) to clarify requirements and resolve issues.\nProvided training, mentoring, and performance feedback to junior QA engineers.\nReviewed test cases, test scenarios, and test execution reports prepared by team members. \nPerformed functional, regression, integration, accessibility, and UAT testing.\nConducted Root Cause Analysis by gathering relevant data related to the defect, including reports, logs, backend etc.\nWriting SQL queries (using SELECT, JOIN, etc.) to extract data and verify that it is correctly stored, updated, or deleted after application actions.\nPerformed Data Migration Testing by running SQL queries against both the source and target databases to compare row-level data and pinpoint any discrepancies.\nComparing the data displayed on the front-end user interface with the data actually stored in the database to ensure accuracy and consistency.\n\n\nProject 3 - Oct 2018 - Jan-2020\nSTAR (Spend Tracking Reports) Reports\n\nTools & Technologies:\nJMeter, Postman, JIRA, MS Office, Notepad++\n\nTeam Size: 5\n\nRole: Module QA Lead\n\nProject Link & Description \t\nSTAR is a product which is used to track all spent information coming from different Polaris products for the same client in the form of various reports. In the STAR product, users can check reports for different countries for related Health Care Providers and Health Care Organisations.\n\nResponsibilities & Achievements:\nDesigned and implemented test cases for functional and regression testing.\nUnderstand the requirement and provide estimations based on that.\nWorked closely with the development team to identify and resolve defects, enhancing the product release quality.\nDocumented test results and reported bugs using JIRA, ensuring timely resolution of issues.\nParticipated in sprint retrospectives to provide quality feedback and identify process improvement opportunities.\nPerformed API Testing with the help of Postman.\nPerformed Load Testing using JMeter.\nInteraction with Client to better understand the customer requirements.\nGive Reverse KT to the client for every new system after taking transition from them.\nMentoring the Junior/newly joined resources.\nPrepared UAT scenarios for Client regarding UAT testing.\n\nProject 4 - Feb 2015 - Sep-2018\nRMS (Request Management System)\n\nTools & Technologies:\nManual Testing, Cross browser testing,  Regression Testing, System Testing.\n\nTeam Size: 8\n\nRole: Sr. QA Engineer\n\nProject Link & Description\t\nGrant management system is a web-based application that provides the funding for the research purpose of incurable disease like cancer. GMS system is used by major leading pharmaceutical clients. All this client helps in research work to life sciences companies/individuals with their compliance, finance, sales and marketing Processes.\n\nResponsibilities & Achievements:\nDesigned and executed test cases for complex web applications. Recognized for maintaining high-quality documentation and test traceability.\nPerformed thorough functional, regression, 