acting, Details of Expenses, Spend on HCP and Activity, Maintaining FMV.\nResponsibilities & Achievements:\nPerform Functional testing on the application.\nUnderstand the requirement and provide estimations based on that.\nAnalyze Test Scenarios from Requirements and write test cases.\nPerform Regression testing.\nPerform Sanity, Integration, Regression and DB Testing of the Application at different levels.\nPerformed API Testing with the help of POSTMAN tool.\nWork closely with the Developers to get updates and resolve defects.\nGood understanding with functional specifications.\nInteraction with Client to better understand the customer requirements.\nActively involved in MOM.\nShare DSR with all Stockholders regarding QA cycle status.\nGive reverse KT to the client for every new system after taking transition from them.\nMentoring the Junior/newly joined resources.\nPrepared UAT scenarios for Client regarding UAT testing.\n\nProject 3 -  Apr 2017 - Jan 2020\vHCPM & IZenda\n\nTools & Technologies\nTesting Methodologies, SQL Server 2008, XML, JIRA\n\nTeam Size : 3\n\nRole : QA Engineer\n\vHCPM provides the Tiering value to the Service Providers from the HCPM system itself to other systems. Tiering is one of the thresholds which helps to identify the Fees of Service Providers taking part within the Activity.\vIZenda is a reporting tool which generally helps to gather data at one place in the form of different reports. End User can have the data for any Activity at any status within the system.\n\nResponsibilities & Achievements:\nPerform Sanity, Functional, Integration, Regression Testing of the Application at different levels.\nAnalyze scenarios from requirements and write Test Cases.\nWork closely with the Developers and Client to get updates and resolve defects.\nResponsible to have all functional specifications.\nActively involved in MOM.\nResponsible to share Status Report with all Stockholders regarding QA cycle.\nResponsible to share QA estimation.\n\n\nProject 4 - Sep 2016 - Mar 2017\vSTAR (Spend Tracking Reports) Reports\n\nTools & Technologies\nTesting Methodologies, SQL Server 2008, XML, TFS\n\nTeam Size : 7\n\nRole : QA Engineer\nSTAR is a product which is used to track all spends information coming from different Polaris products for the same client in the form of various reports. In STAR product, user can check reports for different countries for related Health Care Providers and Health Care Organisations.\n\nResponsibilities & Achievements:\nPerformed Interface testing for 4-5 different projects without having any prior knowledge of them.\nPerform Sanity, Functional, Integration, Regression and DB Testing of the Application at different levels.\nAnalyze scenarios from requirements and write Test Cases.\nWork closely with the Developers and Client to get updates and resolve defects.\nResponsible to have all functional specifications.\nResponsible to interact with Client to have a better understanding for the customer requirements.\nActively involved in MOM.\nResponsible to share Status Report with all Stockholders regarding QA cycle.\nResponsible to share QA estimation.\nResponsible to share Weekly Status Report to QA Manager.\n\n\nProject 5 - Feb 2016 - Apr 2016\nRMS (Request Management System)\n\nGrant management system is a web-based application that provides the funding for the research purpose of incurable disease like cancer. GMS system is used by major leading pharmaceutical clients. All this client helps in research work to life sciences companies/individuals with their compliance, finance, sales and marketing Processes.\n\nTools & Technologies\nTesting Methodologies, SQL Server 2008, XML, TFS\n\nTeam Size : 8\n\nRole : QA Engineer\n\nResponsibilities & Achievements\nPerformed Interface testing.\nPerform Sanity, Functional, Integration, Regression and DB Testing of the Application at different levels.\nAnalyze scenarios from requirements and write Test Cases.\nWork closely with the Developers and Client to