ced in assisting/coordinating with VP/Director/DM.\nPortfolio Accounting and Analysis.\nKnowledge of the IT industry, products, and technologies.\n\nEXPERIENCE\nInfoBeans, Indore, India \nManager - Delivery Office\nFebruary 2016 - Present\nEDUCATION & TRAINING\n\n2014 - 2016\nPGDM in Marketing and IT, Indore\nJaipuria Institute of Management\n\n2010 - 2013\nBachelor of Commerce, RDVV Jabalpur\nG. S. College of Commerce and Economics\n\nPROJECTS\nProject 1 -  February 2016 - March 2018\n\nRole\nPMO Executive\nAssisting Director of Delivery, on the Project-Portfolio Management activities. Coordinating with Finance, HR and Admin teams for data driven decision making which optimizes operational excellence of the delivery unit.\nResponsibilities include:\nMaintaining records of people, projects, invoices.\nWorking with tools and data related to project management metrics.\nCompile timesheet, create invoice drafts and coordinates with Account Receivables (AR) in raising the invoices.\nCoordinate with RMG and delivery managers for resource allocation.\nCoordinate with HR for team member compliance control.\nCoordinates with delivery managers, directors and Vice President and coordinates for smooth project office functions.\n\n\n\n\nProject 2 - April 2018 - March 2021\n\nRole\nAssistant Manager - Project Office\nAssistant Manager – Project Office: manages project office functions, implementing processes and compliances within the group. The aim is to work together with the organizational pillars such as Finance, HR and Admin to achieve project office excellence by monitoring and controlling the activities along with a larger aim to apply the processes throughout the organization.\nResponsibilities includes:\nManaging Project Office\nContracts\nCommercials\nResource Management\nAccounting\nInvoicing\nProcess\nCompliance\nGovernance\nReporting\n\nProject 3 - April 2021 - July 2022\n\nTools & Technologies\nWorked on InfoBeans internal tools based in C#, .Net, MVC, SQL, Salesforce\n\nRole\nManager - Delivery Office\nManager - Delivery Office: orchestrator of the delivery unit processes, compliance, monitoring, and control. The aim is to achieve DU operative excellence by executing strategies aligned with organization goals. \nResponsibilities includes:\nManagement of inhouse Accounting & Invoicing, Project, and Resource Management tools.\nCoordinating Change, Enhancements, and Bug Fixes of these tools.\nKnowledge execution of the inhouse tools throughout the organization.\nCoordinating the integration task of multifunctional internal tools.\nCreating and documenting monthly DU based accounting reports.\nMapping opportunities through resource management.\nContract Management.\n\nMajor Projects:\nAccounting & Invoicing, Project, and Resource Management tools.\nI was responsible for overseeing the improvements and enhancements of these tools and establishing them throughout the organization.\nI coordinated with the project sponsor, delivery managers, project managers, leads, finance team and HR team to gather inputs and convert them into requirements which were eventually implemented in the tools.\nCoordinated bug fixes and enhancement on time and within budget.\nEducated end users which increased the usability of these tools by 45%.\nAchieved 65% scalability of the tools.\nThe internal tools are now better than before with new features, enhancements and improved UI. Built in such a way that it can be easily integrated with other inhouse tools.\nCentral Repository: A salesforce-based application to store data and documents related to Projects which are visible to Clients in order to maintain fair transparency. It includes Projects, MSA, SOW, Invoices and other related data and documents.\n\n\n\n\n\nProject 4 - July 2022 - December 2025\n\nTools & Technologies\nMS Office, Salesforce (CSM), Confluence, Jira. Understanding on Basic AWS Infrastructure and DevOps.\n\nRole\nProject Manager\nUnder this position worked with the cross functional teams, interacting with business counterparts, project planning, execution, tracking updates, utilized AI-driven predictive analytics to identify potential bottlenecks in software releases, reducing project slippage, resource planning, ensuring on time delivery with quality deliverables.\n\nResponsibilities includes:\nManage projects and software releases from beginning to the end.\nOversee project planning, scheduling, and implementation to ensure timely completion within budget.\nProduce, update, and present project management artifacts.\nManage backlogs in Jira of projects running on Agile methodology.\nManage project expectations with team members and client stakeholders.\nCommunicate to customer stakeholders regarding project progress, issue management, risk management, timelines, and escalations.\nManage timeline, cost, and quality metrics for projects in my portfolio.\nManage releases and cutover plans.\nEnsure compliance with service level agreements, customer change controls and SDLC components.\nDrive desired professional behaviors and motivate the team to the highest levels of performance.\nEnsure that team members have the best conditions to perform successfully, advocate for positive change and flag risks and problems.\nManage the client relationship throughout the engagement.\nContinually assess people, process and technology risks and adjust project plans to address them accordingly.\n\nAchievements:\nSuccessfully managed and delivered 150+ projects / software releases, achieving 94% deliveries under SLA. \nSuccessfully orchestrated cloud based major / minor software upgrades / patches for 40+ global clients with a 94% customer satisfaction.\nLead cross-functional teams, fostering collaboration and effective communication, ensuring 96% efficient deliveries.\n\n\n\nSKILLS\nProject Management\n(3/5)\n\nProcess & Compliance\n(4/5)\n\nSDLC & Agile Methodologies\n(3/5)\n\nProject Monitor, Control & Reports\n(4/5)\n\nContracts & Commercials\n(4/5)\n\nResource M