e Domain\nExpertise in designing, developing, integrating, executing, testing, and debugging as well as performing modifications in existing code to add new features\nEXPERIENCE\nInfoBeans, Pune, India \nTechnical Architect - Software\nApril 2019 - Present\nInfoBeans, Indore, India \nSr Software Engg - Software\nDec 2016 - Mar 2019\nEDUCATION & TRAINING\n\n2007\nB.Tech (Computer Science & Engg), UPTU, Lucknow\nG.L.A institute of Technology and Mgmt, Mathura\n\n2003\nHigher Secondary School, CBSE Agra\nSt. Augustine School.\n\n2001\nHigh School Certificate, CBSE Agra\nSt. Augustine School.\nPROJECTS\n\nProject 1 - Mar 2025 -Present\n Stanza by InfoBeans\n\nTools & Technologies\nC# (.NET 8, Visual Studio 2022), MVC, Web API, Postgresql, Github\n\nTeam Size\n10\n\nRole\nSoftware Engineer\n\nProject Link\n https://stanzacsainfob2cwebapp.azurewebsites.net/\n\nStanza offers a collaborative platform for managing committees, developing standards, and conducting voting and balloting. It assists in centralizing essential business operations and gives a comprehensive overview of the tasks that staff and members need to undertake. With its user-friendly and intuitive design, teams can utilize it with little oversight.\n\nResponsibilities & Achievements:\nInvolved in designing new features/Requirement\nCommittee Management\nStandards Management\nMembership Management\n\nProject 2 - Nov 2019 - Jan 2025\n  NetApp SnapCenter Software - Data Backup Management\n\nTools & Technologies\nC++11/14, Win32 API, C# (.NET 8, Visual Studio 2022), MVC, Rest API, ONTAP Storage, Git\n\nTeam Size\n12\n\nRole\nSoftware Engineer\n\nProject Link\nhttps://docs.netapp.com/us-en/snapcenter/\n\nNetApp SnapCenter Software is a simple, centralized, scalable platform that provides application-consistent data protection for applications, databases, host file systems, and VMs running on ONTAP systems\n\nResponsibilities & Achievements:\nInvolved in designing new features/Requirement in many NetApp SnapCenter Plug-ins\no SnapCenter Plug-in for Oracle Database\no SnapCenter Plug-in for Microsoft Windows\no SnapCenter Plug-in for Microsoft Exchange Server\no SnapCenter Plug-in for Microsoft SQL\no SnapCenter Plug-in for VMware vSphere\n\n\nProject 3 - Jan 2017 - Oct 2019\n SMI-S Provider (Storage Management Initiative Specification)\n\nTools & Technologies\nC,C++,Win32 API, Visual Studio 2010, Perforce\n\nTeam Size\n2\n\nRole\nSoftware Engineer\n\nProject Link\nhttps://library.netapp.com/ecmdocs/ECMLP2608866/html/GUID-EE384353-6024-4CEA-AD57-6BB590E6791C.html\n\nNetApp Storage Management Initiative Specification (SMI-S) Provider (formerly Data ONTAP® SMI-S Agent) is a command-based interface that detects and manages platforms that run ONTAP® software. It uses Web-Based Enterprise Management (WBEM) protocols to manage, monitor, and report about storage elements by type. SMI-S Provider follows schemas standardized by two organizations: Distributed Management Task Force (DMTF) and Storage Networking Industry Association (SNIA).You can install SMI-S Provider on a Microsoft® Windows® host or a Linux® host\n\nResponsibilities & Achievements:\nEmbedded Systems Programming in C/C++ under Windows and Linux environment.\nInvolved in design phase and Debugging of multiple new features/Requirement of SMI-S Provider.\nInvolved in the software product development life cycle, including analysis, designing, coding, testing and implementation.\n\nProject 4 - Aug 2017 - Oct 2019\nOnCommand Plug-in for Microsoft\n\nTools & Technologies\nC#, Visual Studio 2012, SCOM 2012/2016\n\nTeam Size \n2\n\nRole\nSoftware Engineer\n\nProject Link\nhttps://www.netapp.com/us/products/management-software/oncommand-plug-ins-for-microsoft.aspx\n\nOnCommand Plug-in for Microsoft is an enterprise-class storage monitoring and application that integrates with Microsoft System Center Operations Manager (SCOM). The plug-in enables administrators to Monitor, manage and report on storage. Plots system performance me