78,0.71086526,-0.6415617,-0.80600464,-2.4602685,0.8262362,-1.8593333,-0.19679855,0.78636974,1.9268394,0.9535413,1.1283176,0.424495,0.08014323,0.5374283,-0.65003157,-1.0752987,-2.7614303,-0.38154086,-0.5993545,-0.056386482,0.24227047,0.66571575,-0.12495301,1.2054217,-2.0910482,0.7983016,0.016031908,0.7478074,-2.5579042,0.08608424,0.22408134,-0.87020445,-0.877838,-1.0984687,-0.5531739,-2.3966336,1.3673334,-1.880724]	Designation: Software Engineer\nLocation: Mumbai\nWork Mode: wfo\nExperience: 73 months\nSkills: ASP .Net, C#, SQL, OOPS, HTML, CSS, ASP .Net Core\nCertifications: Cisco Specialist for ASP .Net\nResume Content: \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t      A PROUD MEMBER OF \nKratika Patil                                                      \nSoftware Engineer\n7 years of Industry Experience\nDevelopment, Research & Analysis\n\n\nOVERVIEW\nInnovative and multi-disciplinary developer with hands-on experience in development, database design, user interfaces, analyzing and managing requirements. I love solving problems that result in delightful and innovative experiences. Overall 6.9 years of industry experience across software development and client communication.\n\nPassionate for developing and designing information architecture with a focus on developing functional & usable products.\nInnovative team player with a passion for continuous learning and utilizing honed skills to develop software applications.\nExperience in client relationship management and client communication.\nEDUCATION & TRAINING\n\n2017\nB.E. in Computer Science, RGPV\nTRUBA College of Engineering & Technology, Indore\n\n\n\n\nPROJECTS\n\nProject 1 - Jan 2019 - Feb 2020\nInvestigator Initiated Study Management System\n\nTools & Technologies\nAsp.Net  with C#, VSTS, SSMS, TFS, JIRA, Agile Methodology\n\nTeam Size\n8\n\nRole\nTrainee Software Engineer\n\nProject Link\nNA\n\nThe IIS system assists life science companies in managing the complexities associated with managing Investigator Initiated Studies. The tool ensures compliance with the various regulations that apply to IIS funding, including ABAC, transparency and clinical trial guidelines. IIS improves the strategic alignment of resources, and ensures compliance with ever shifting global disclosure requirements. The solution gives life science companies an automated, secure and compliant system to manage these multiple demands.\n\n\nResponsibilities & Achievements:\nRequirement analysis and Project planning.\nModule designing and customizations.\nDeveloping and managing customization Projects.\n\n\nProject 2 - Mar 2020 - Present\nRequest Management System \n\nTools & Technologies\nAsp.Net  with C#, VSTS, SSMS, TFS, Agile Methodology\n\nTeam Size\n8\n\nRole\nSoftware Engineer\n\nProject Link\nNA\n\nRequest Management System (RMS) effectively manages the external grant request submission and approval process for multiple activity types in an ever-shifting regulatory environment. RMS allows organizations to easily track and report on a variety of request activities, providing requestors, approvers, and administrators full visibility into the grant processing lifecycle. RMS tracks the entire workflow of a grant request including registration, request submission, review and approval, contracting (electronic LOA) and payment, outcomes and financial reconciliation, and custom reporting.\n\nResponsibilities & Achievements\nRequirement analysis and Project planning.\nModule designing and customizations.\nDeveloping and managing customization Projects.\n\nSKILLS\nASP.Net & C#\n(4/5)\n\nREST API\n(3.5/5)\n\nASP.Net MVC \n(3.5/5)\n\nASP.Net Core\n(3/5)\n\nDatabase Design & SQL Server\n(4/5)\n\nHTML & CSS\n(4/5)\n\nASP.NET Web Forms\n(4/5)\n\nJavaScript\n(3.5/5)\n\nAgile Methodology\n(4/5)\n\n\nTOOLS\nMicrosoft Visual studio,Eclipse, VSTS, SSMS, SQL Profiler, Confluence & JIRA\nMANAGERIAL EXPERIENCE\nNA\nDOMAIN\nHealthcare\nEducation\n\nLANGUAGES\nEnglish\nHindi\n\n\n\nProject 3 - Nov 2024 - Present\nHealthcare Interaction Po