ckend services for real-time bank transaction data processing.\nImplemented features for reconciliation, validation, and automated accounting entries, reducing manual effort and improving financial accuracy.\nEnhanced the system to support mapping of live AWB (Air Waybill) invoices in the logistics module, ensuring accurate tracking and reconciliation with financial data.\nCollaborated with finance and logistics stakeholders to align application workflows with business and compliance requirements.\n\nSecurity Fixes:\n Identifying and addressing security vulnerabilities across various systems, ensuring that sensitive customer and operational data is protected.\n This includes implementing best practices such as data encryption, secure authentication, and safeguarding against potential threats like SQL injection and cross-site scripting (XSS).\n\n\nProject 2 - Jan 2023 - July 2023\nStanza\n\nTools & Technologies\nC#, .NET APIs, Entity Framework, SQL Server, Git, Postman, LINQ\n\n\nTeam Size\n2\n\nRole\n.Net Developer\n\nDescription \t\nA web-based system providing access to some standards balloƟng tools & informaƟon as well as\nthe rules associated with forming a standards balloƟng group. It would allow people to vote for it.\n\n\nProject 3-March 2022- Nov 2022\nIQVIA\n\nTools & Technologies\nC#, ASP.NET Core, configurations\n\nTeam Size\n2\n\nRole\nBackend Developer\n\nDescription\nIQVIA is a global leader in healthcare data analytics, providing cutting-edge solutions that help pharmaceutical companies, healthcare providers, and research organizations improve decision-making and enhance patient outcomes. The project I worked on was focused on building scalable, secure, and high-performance backend systems that support the analysis and processing of large healthcare datasets.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nSkills\n\nDotnet\n(4/5)\n\nSQL Server\n(3.7/5)\n\nDot net Core\n(4/5)\n\nC#\n(3.7/5)\n\nHTML5 & CSS\n(3.5/5)\n\nAjax & JavaScript\n(3.2/5)\n\n\nClient Interaction \n(3.8/5)\n\nTe