pplication.\nFamiliar with Git and its commands have hands-on experience on it.\nUsed OOPS concept while developing the applications and followed standard code practices.\nUnderstanding of performance and efficiency with strong problem solving and troubleshooting skills.\n\n\n\nCURRENT ORGANIZATION\n Software Engineer, Infobeans Technologies Pvt Ltd\nPREVIOUS ORGANIZATION\n System Engineer, Tata Consultancy Services (Feb 2020-June 2022)\n\nEDUCATION & TRAINING\n\n2018\nBachelor of Engineering, CSE, RGPV\nAcropolis Institute of Technology & Research, Indore(MP)\nPROJECTS\nProject 5 - June 2024 - August 2025\nVirtual Storage/ Data Infrastructure Services \n\nTools & Technologies\nPython, Vmware, Esxi hosts, KVM hosts, SSH, Virtualisation storage and tools, Putty, Linux, Git. \nTeam Size\n5\n\nRole\nPython Developer\n\nProject Link\nNDA\n\nOverview\nThis is a storage virtualisation and data infrastructure project. This client provides virtual infrastructure like compute and storage to the customers so that they can run their applications on it.\nMy role in this project was to provide seamless access of the product to the existing customers. I was responsible to solve the customer’s problem if they face any issue while using the product.\nTo do the RCA, To rectify if the problem is due to configuration issue or a defect in product. If there is a bug in the product and need to enhance the product then I do the needful.\n\nProject 4 - December 2022 - May 2024\nPublication Portal/ News Portal \n\nTools & Technologies\nPython, Django, AWS, Jenkins, Docker, Pycharm, HTML, CSS, Javascript, Postman, Cron Server, Celery.\n\nTeam Size\n3\nRole\nPython Developer\n\nProject Link\nNDA\n\nOverview\nThis is a web application project and domain is the publication portal and news portal. The client sites are accessed in around more than 20 countries. \nThis is an already existing project where my job is  to develop new functionalities and to maintain the existing functionalities.\nWe are using Python, Django, AWS, HTML, CSS, Javascript, Docker and Jenkins to develop, maintain and to deploy the application.\nWe use Agile Methodology and Assembla(Client Internal) ticket portal to track the task. \nI am mainly working on Python, Django and AWS services like S3, Dynamodb, SQS, SES, EC2, Lambda, ECS, ACM etc.\nI also have some hands-on experience using Docker, Jenkins and Cron while deploying the application on the Server/ Production.\n\nProject 3 - August 2022 - November 2022\nTech Education \n\nTools & Technologies\nPython, Numpy, Pandas, VSCode, Anaconda, Jupyter\n\nTeam Size\n2\n\nRole\nPython Developer\n\nProject Link\nNDA\n\nOverview\nThe client wants to analyze its own client data so he needs the data in a segregated form by using python pandas and numpy.\nMy job was to create multiple python scripts  which will retrieve millions of client records from the client database and store it into a CSV file or Dynamodb table.\nAfter storing those raw data into CSV/Dynamodb now I have to write a scripts using pandas and numpy where data will get segregated according to the conditions given and the segregated data gets stored into the dataframes. Once all the conditions are fulfilled at the end the data frames will get merged into a single data frame which in the end will be converted to a CSV file or stored into a Dynamodb table. Now this segregated and filtered data can be used by client for further analyses using tools like Power BI.\n\n\nProject 2 - June 2021 - June 2022\nBanking Financial Project (BFSI Domain)\n\nTools & Technologies\nPython, AWS(DynamoDb, S3 Bucket,Lambda etc), JIRA , PyCharm and Eclipse for Development & automation,Jenkins,Postman, SwaggerHub\n\nTeam Size\n11\n\nRole\nPython Developer\n\nProject Link\nNDA\n\nOverview\nThe organization was creating and upgrading the old on-premise financial portal system to a new cloud based app system. According to the government norms new Pension Schemes were introduced and accordingly the organization had to create a new application for the same. We have created a new application on the cloud and the existing application was shifted from on-premise to cloud.\nMy role was to develop the Rest Api using the Python Flask and connecting it with the AWS Dynamodb table and S3 Bucket for the internal use of the project and to develop the Python Automation scripts for the QA team.\nWhile developing the application I have also implemented automatic scripts for file reading,writing and transferring from local to S3 bucket and vis-a-vis.\n\nProject 1 - May 2020 - June 2021\nBanking Finance Project (BFSI Domain)\n\nTools & Technologies\nPython, AWS(DynamoDb, S3 Bucket,Lambda etc), JIRA, PyCharm \nand Eclipse  for Development & automation,Jenkins,Postman, SwaggerHub.\n\nTeam Size\n8\n\nRole\nPython Developer\n\nProject Link\nNDA\n\nOverview\nIt was a banking finance project where the users can use the bank platform for stock market and other financial related activities.\nMy role was to develop a user-friendly Python Automation Framework for its data driven Rest Api automation testing which can have a better testing report and easy to understand scripts for the QA team.\nI have developed a user-friendly key driven Python Robot Automation Framework using the Robot framework library of Python to simplify and enhance the automation testing for the rest of the users.\nPython Libraries that I have used are Robotframework, Json, Logger, OS, Regex etc.\nThe AWS Python library used was Boto3. I have used this library for Session connection , Dynamodb table creation and uploading ,retrieving and transfer of  files from various S3 buckets.\n\n\n\n\n\nSKILLS\nPython Development\n(4.0/5)\n\nDjango Framework\n(4.0/5)\n\nFlask Framework\n(3.5/5)\n\nAmazon Web Services\n(4.0/5)\n\nSQL Databases(MySQL,Postgres,SQLite)\n(4.0/5)\n\nREST API\n(4/5)\n\nHTML/CSS/JavaScript\n(3.5/5)\n\nDockers/Jenkins\n(3.0/5)\n\nAgile Methodology\n(4/5)\n\nCommunication Skills\n(4/5)\nTOOLS\nJira, PyCharm,